Connect with us\nDepartments\nCivil and Environmental Engineering\nCivil and Environmental Engineering Doctoral Program\nCivil and Environmental Engineering Doctoral Program\nMake a Lasting Impact Through Research and Innovation in Civil & Environmental Engineering\nThe Ph.D. in Civil and Environmental Engineering at SMU\u2019s Lyle School of Engineering prepares students for careers in advanced research, academia, industry, and public service. The program emphasizes independent, original research under close faculty mentorship, supported by advanced coursework tailored to each student\u2019s area of specialization. Doctoral students develop the technical depth, analytical rigor, and scholarly expertise needed to address complex challenges in infrastructure systems, environmental sustainability, and resilient engineering solutions.\nApply View Catalog\nTake Your Next Step\nApply Now\nApply Now\nLearn about admission requirements, application materials, deadlines, and funding opportunities for the Civil and Environmental Engineering Ph.D. program.\nDepartment Research\nDepartment Research\nDiscover the research areas, labs, and projects shaping innovation in civil and environmental engineering at SMU.\nDepartment Faculty\nDepartment Faculty\nWork closely with nationally recognized faculty whose expertise spans civil infrastructure, environmental systems, and interdisciplinary research.\nBack to top\nLyle School of Engineering\nLyle School of Engineering\n3101 Dyer Street\nDallas, TX 75205\n214-768-3050\nQuick links\nABET accreditation\nSACSCOC Accreditation\nFollow Us\nFacebook\nTwitter\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nYouTube\nApply Now\nSchedule a Visit\nRequest Info\nSMU Home\n\u00a9 Southern Methodist University\nPrimary navigation menu\nClose Menu\nSearch\nAbout Lyle\nOur Namesake: Bobby B. Lyle\nFaculty Directory\nLabs and Spaces\nMission Statement\nDean's Office\nGiving to Lyle\nContact\nLyle Curriculum Committee\nUndergraduate\nAdvising\nB.S. in computer science\nB.S. i